"SQ-02","2","Find the wolf, identify the apparent survivor and recover a route home.","Match landmarks, search the burned homestead and pursue the ridge silhouette.","Burned homestead, eastern ridge and surviving portal cave","The pen is empty, the figure evades him and every block trace implies one location rather than a copy.","A second crossing ejects him before the portal was built.","He gains a possible culprit but becomes stranded in his own recent past.","Future loss becomes past opportunity under constraint.","210","Use matched compositions and one distant silhouette; conceal the wolf through terrain rather than editing deception."
"SQ-03","3","Warn the younger self and protect the wolf without stopping the journey.","Observe from cover, use local red wool as an indirect route marker and compare remembered cave details.","Pre-discovery homestead perimeter and bare portal cave","The younger self remains close; an explicit warning risks preventing entry; the incomplete marker is already part of memory.","His intervention proves participation, and the remembered frame details identify him as the necessary builder.","He chooses portal construction as the only rescue path he can support with evidence.","Hope of rewriting becomes responsibility for the known chain.","270","Restrict double-avatar overlap to sight lines, silhouettes and younger-self inserts."
"SQ-04","4","Complete the portal before the younger self arrives and preserve the foreknowledge-producing entry.","Mine local obsidian, copy the irregular construction and hide during the opening encounter.","Lava shelf, portal cave and concealment ledge","Time pressure encourages temporary spruce staging beside a route connected to the timber stair.","Lighting the solution to the mystery also creates the proposed cause of the fire.","The younger self enters; the older self sees smoke and races towards the house.","Builder mystery resolves while latent danger becomes immediate.","270","The candidate ignition geometry must be mechanically tested before construction continuity is locked."
"SQ-05","5","Prevent the known ruin, then save what remains meaningfully possible.","Fight the structure fire, recognise the failed resource allocation, redirect water to the eastern drain and release the wolf.","Burning homestead, wolf pen, eastern drain and ridge","Separated fire fronts consume the house; the wolf is seated behind a blocked yard; the arriving earlier self must not see it.","He abandons the roof, saves the wolf and deliberately becomes the silhouette that motivated him.","The ruin remains unchanged, the wolf survives and the portal is extinguished after the required crossing.","Fixed physical loss becomes chosen relational preservation.","270","Rehearse staged fire progression, water placement, wolf pathing, ridge occlusion and portal dousing separately."

